Safety in Academic Chemistry Laboratories — ACS, eighth edition (@gc-acs: 0, is #reference, #part-of @gc-sources) { r_1GAGRBYCJGJAY86HQCNE9S66EP
American Chemical Society Joint Board–Council Committee on Chemical Safety; David C. Finster, editor, and contributors. Safety in Academic Chemistry Laboratories: Best Practices for First- and Second-Year University Students, eighth edition, 2017. ISBN 978-0-8412-3732-2. [Official freely available PDF](https://www.acs.org/content/dam/pldp/center/lab-safety/publications/safety-in-academic-chemistry-laboratories-students.pdf).

Read the entire 76-file-page publication before practical laboratory work, then return to the sections relevant to the actual activity. Its chapters develop laboratory responsibility, chemical hazards, common techniques, equipment, and response through RAMP: recognize hazards, assess risks, minimize risks, and prepare for emergencies. Use it with current institution/procedure-specific assessment and training.

The publication is freely supplied by ACS and states copyright/all rights reserved. It is not represented as an openly licensed adaptation source or a complete statement of current law. Preserve its authorship and notices and use the authorized link. Edition, title/copyright pages, contents, and access checked on 29 October 2026. No PDF is bundled.

